# Copy to .env.local for development, and set the same values in your host's
# dashboard (Vercel/Netlify → Project → Environment Variables) for production.
#
# The site builds and runs with NONE of these set. Each one switches on a
# specific capability, and nothing third-party loads until you opt in.
#
# NOTE: NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are compiled into the build, so changing one
# requires a redeploy, not just a save.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- site

# Canonical origin, no trailing slash. Used for canonical URLs, sitemap.xml,
# robots.txt and Open Graph tags. Set this before launch or search engines will
# index the placeholder domain.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://bizwisetech.com

# Set to "true" on preview/staging deployments so robots.txt blocks crawlers
# and your staging copy never competes with production in search results.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NOINDEX=true

# ------------------------------------------------------- contact details
#
# These can also live in src/content/site.ts. Set them either way — anything
# left blank is HIDDEN across the site rather than rendered as a dead link, so
# no empty "Call us" button ever ships.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=hello@bizwisetech.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_PHONE=+14155551234          # E.164, used for tel: links
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_PHONE_DISPLAY=(415) 555-1234 # how it reads on screen
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_ENABLED=true                # only if that number has WhatsApp

# ------------------------------------------------- contact form delivery
#
# Configure AT LEAST ONE of the two channels below, or the form will tell
# visitors to contact you another way (it never silently drops an enquiry).

# Option 1 — email via Resend (https://resend.com). Free tier is ample for a
# contact form. LEAD_TO_EMAIL accepts a comma-separated list.
#
# NO DOMAIN YET? Sign up to Resend using the SAME address you want enquiries
# sent to, then use onboarding@resend.dev as the sender. Resend's sandbox only
# delivers to the address the account was created with, which is fine when that
# address is you — and it needs no DNS setup at all:
#
#   RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#   LEAD_TO_EMAIL=you@gmail.com          # the address you signed up with
#   LEAD_FROM_EMAIL=onboarding@resend.dev
#
# ONCE YOU HAVE A DOMAIN, verify it with Resend and switch the sender to it.
# Only then can you deliver to any address other than your own, and mail from
# your own domain is far less likely to land in spam.
#
#   LEAD_FROM_EMAIL=website@bizwisetech.com
#
# Never commit the destination address to this repository if it is public —
# set LEAD_TO_EMAIL in your host's dashboard instead. It is server-side only
# and is never exposed to the browser.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# LEAD_TO_EMAIL=hello@bizwisetech.com
# LEAD_FROM_EMAIL=website@bizwisetech.com

# Option 2 — POST the lead as JSON to a CRM, Zapier, Make, HubSpot or Slack.
# Works alongside email; both fire, and either one succeeding is enough.
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/000000/xxxxxx
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_SECRET=some-shared-secret   # sent as the X-Webhook-Secret header

# ------------------------------------------------------- booking widget

# A Calendly / Cal.com / SavvyCal link. When set, the contact page swaps its
# placeholder card for a live scheduling embed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL=https://cal.com/yourname/30min

# ------------------------------------------------------------ analytics
#
# Nothing loads unless set. If you serve EU/UK visitors, gate these behind a
# consent banner before switching them on.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX
# NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=000000000000000

# --------------------------------------------------------- payments (Razorpay)
#
# OPTIONAL. With these unset, "Pay now" says payments aren't switched on and
# links to the contact form — nothing breaks.
#
# THE KEYS ALONE ARE ENOUGH to take a single payment: with KEY_ID and
# KEY_SECRET set, "Pay now" runs Standard Checkout against a one-off ORDER and
# charges one month. That needs no plan and no e-mandate, so it works on a
# fresh test account.
#
# Add a PLAN id for a tier and that tier upgrades to a real recurring
# SUBSCRIPTION instead. Create plans in the Razorpay dashboard, not in this
# repo: the price a customer is charged then lives with the payment provider,
# and a bug here cannot change what someone is billed.
#
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxx
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx   # NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_
# RAZORPAY_PLAN_STARTER=plan_xxxxxxxxxxxx    # the ₹999/month plan
# RAZORPAY_PLAN_GROWTH=plan_xxxxxxxxxxxx     # the ₹1,999/month plan
#
# Webhook: point Razorpay at https://your-domain/api/razorpay/webhook and
# subscribe to subscription.charged, subscription.halted and payment.failed.
# The secret below is the one you type into that webhook form.
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# Use rzp_test_ keys until you are ready. Live keys require completed KYC on
# the Razorpay account, and recurring payments need e-mandate/UPI AutoPay
# enabled on it — ask Razorpay support if the subscription call is rejected.
